invariant: INV-16
file: record.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_host
reason: the record layer seals every ChaCha20-Poly1305 record under the probe's
  bit alone, whatever the direction's cpu states, so a caller that stated
  the multiply's timing gets the slow copy on every record it seals and
  the bit picks nothing there. The tags are the same.
  test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h requires a handshake between two ends
  whose ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to call no file
  under its own names.

--- old
    AEAD_SEAL_CPU(d->cpu, d->key, nonce, hdr, REC_HDR, body, len, body, body + len);
--- new
    AEAD_SEAL_CPU(CH_CPU_PROBED, d->key, nonce, hdr, REC_HDR, body, len, body, body + len);
